<Layout title="Architectural Design Tools & Resources | ATECT Architecture" description="Architectural design tools, documentation resources, and workflow guidance for homeowners, builders, contractors, and design professionals.">
  <section class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Resources / Design & Documentation</p><h1>Architectural Design Tools</h1><p>Resources for planning, visualization, drawing, specifications, and construction documentation—organized around how a project moves from idea to buildable information.</p></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Design Knowledge</p><h2>Start with the information your project needs.</h2></div><p class="section-intro">Good tools support clear decisions. They do not replace the architectural thinking that connects site, program, materials, structure, and construction.</p></div>
    <div class="resource-list">
      <a href="/resources/architectural-drawings-vs-construction-drawings"><strong>Architectural Drawings vs. Construction Drawings</strong><span>Understand the difference between design communication and build-ready documentation.</span></a>
      <a href="/resources/what-should-be-included-construction-document-set"><strong>What Should Be Included in a Construction Document Set?</strong><span>A practical overview of the information contractors need to price and build a project.</span></a>
      <a href="/resources/what-to-know-before-home-addition"><strong>What to Know Before Starting a Home Addition</strong><span>Key planning questions to consider before design and construction begin.</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section alt"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">ATECT Approach</p><h2>Tools are part of the process.</h2></div><p class="section-intro">ATECT Architecture combines design development, visualization, construction documentation, and coordination to create clearer project information.</p></div><a class="button dark" href="/contact">Start a Project</a></section>
</Layout>
<style>
.resource-list{display:grid;gap:12px}.resource-list a{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:30px;padding:28px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.resource-list strong{font:600 23px/1.25 Manrope}.resource-list span{color:var(--muted)}@media(max-width:700px){.resource-list a{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:8px}}
</style>